+## Final A4 recovery sweep and readiness
+
+The temporary token watermark proposal was rejected during the personal semantic sweep: Herdr restart between reservation/data requests followed by producer crash can erase the recovery token while leaving new sequence history. The final contract uses one feature-owned persisted counter per socket/pane, reserved before IPC; existing managed integration stays untouched. First-install provisioning is explicit, missing/corrupt state fails closed, and rollback preserves counters. This answers A4 and its adjacent R1/R11/R12/R14/R15/R17 clauses without adding a service or weakening any method. File-store design is prospective; the policy model is not an implemented extension.
+
+Primary filesystem support: Node fs API and POSIX rename retrieved in this pass; source URLs, retrieval times and exact hashes are in amendment/filesystem-sources.json. Both complete fetched references were opened for source checks; no live state store was created. Node exposes open/sync/rename; POSIX specifies atomic rename. The original web extraction backend refused extraction, so direct official retrieval supplied the source, not the failed attempt.
+
+All 15 amendment rule groups attended; full document and cross-references checked personally, no agent dispatched. Scope remains specification/evidence only; no library/application diff, runtime mutation, provider call, installation, reload, commit, push or merge.
